#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166633 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166795 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1df2e164-251d-5ea1-a49a-fe5bc8d67ae6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Function Using the Hyperbolic Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/id #uuid "2281e86d-4f21-53da-b6fa-1f178d4862a5" :question/math-academy-id "e-8433" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nCalculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\dfrac{1}{1+\\sinh^2 x} \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the Pythagorean identity \n\n$$\n\\cos^2 x + \\sin^2 x= 1.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n\\cosh^2x -\\sinh^2x=1\n$$\n\nwhich we can write as\n\n$$\n1+\\sinh^2x=\\cosh^2x.\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we have\n\n$$\n\\sech x = \\dfrac{1}{\\cosh x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the denominator and calculate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x})}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sech}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166634 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166796 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "97c01757-f2bf-5b7b-b51b-ff490b54f555" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Function Using the Hyperbolic Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/id #uuid "9b63d35a-f1c5-554f-ac4c-68d18afa153a" :question/math-academy-id "e-8434" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{\\ln 2} \\dfrac{\\tanh{x}-\\tanh^3{x}}{\\sech{x}} \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the secant-tangent identity \n\n$$\n1 + \\tan^2 x= \\sec^2{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic secant-tangent identity\n\n$$\n1-\\tanh^2x=\\sech^2{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the integral and evaluate it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\frac{\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x-{tanh}^{3}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sech}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\frac{(1-{tanh}^{2}⁡x)\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sech}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\frac{{sech}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sech}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sech}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)+\\operatorname{sech}⁡0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}}+\\frac{2}{{e}^{0}+{e}^{0}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{(2+\\frac{1}{2})}+1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{(\\frac{5}{2})}+1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{5}+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166635 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166797 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5f377f3-700a-57a9-96e5-954aed678e62" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Function Using the Hyperbolic Cosecant-Cotangent Identity"}] :question/id #uuid "7af9f5f6-1e14-55ea-8a09-25d211cb40d8" :question/math-academy-id "e-8435" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{\\ln 3}^{\\ln 6} \\dfrac{\\csch{x}}{\\coth^2{x} - 1} \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the cosecant-cotangent identity \n\n$$\n\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}\n1 + \\cot^2 x= \\csc^2{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic cosecant-cotangent identity\n\n$$\n\\coth^2x - 1=\\csch^2{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the integral and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int_{\\ln 3}^{\\ln 6} \\dfrac{\\csch{x}}{\\coth^2{x} - 1} \\, \\textrm{d}x\n\t\t\t&= \\int_{\\ln 3}^{\\ln 6} \\dfrac{\\csch{x}}{\\csch^2{x}} \\, \\textrm{d}x \\[5pt]\n\t\t\t&= \\int_{\\ln 3}^{\\ln 6} \\sinh{x} \\, \\textrm{d}x \\[5pt]\n\t\t\t&= \\cosh{x} \\Big|_{\\ln 3}^{\\ln 6}\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t&= \\cosh(\\ln 6) - \\cosh(\\ln 3)\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t&= \\left(\\dfrac{e^{\\ln 6}+e^{-\\ln 6}}{2}\\right) - \\left(\\dfrac{e^{\\ln 3}+e^{-\\ln 3}}{2}\\right)\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t&= \\left(\\dfrac{6 + \\dfrac{1}{6}}{2}\\right) - \\left(\\dfrac{3 + \\dfrac{1}{3}}{2}\\right)\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t&= \\dfrac{37}{12} - \\dfrac{5}{3}\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t&= \\dfrac{37}{12} - \\dfrac{20}{12} \\[5pt]\n            &= \\dfrac{17}{12}\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166636 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166798 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a95e37c6-66f4-5a70-87e8-31f3694a20a4" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Hyperbolic Functions With Linear Arguments"}] :question/id #uuid "14733493-2ad9-5fc2-9afe-26384f6ce9ed" :question/math-academy-id "e-8436" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int \\dfrac{2}{\\cosh^2(2x+1)-1} \\, \\textrm{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n\\cos^2 \\theta + \\sin^2 \\theta = 1.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n\\cosh^2 \\theta - \\sinh^2 \\theta = 1.\n$$\n\nSetting $\\theta = 2x + 1,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\cosh^2 (2x+1) - \\sinh^2(2x+1) = 1\n$$\n\nwhich can be written as\n\n$$\n\\cosh^2 (2x+1) -1 = \\sinh^2(2x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{{cosh}^{2}⁡(2x+1)-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{{sinh}^{2}⁡(2x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int {csch}^{2}⁡(2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{coth}⁡(2x+1)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186537900 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166795 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1df2e164-251d-5ea1-a49a-fe5bc8d67ae6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Function Using the Hyperbolic Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a908713-5ac5-5134-a0e7-86afc9750420" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537315} {:answer/id #uuid "4f3c99bb-9d3b-5885-8411-3a5f94462ecf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537392} {:answer/id #uuid "7ac49e22-956a-5757-b843-898b336ff080" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{csch}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537469} {:answer/id #uuid "d67bbc9b-a120-5ae6-be39-d2884fe54ab0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537656} {:answer/id #uuid "fedaa517-46ad-50d1-9223-915aeb1842d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537753}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a908713-5ac5-5134-a0e7-86afc9750420" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537315} :answer-field/id #uuid "bef0a448-ccbc-545d-a9c9-133e5c77b5fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537851}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "347de47e-5245-5fd2-b46a-2d80ee9ca643" :question/math-academy-id "q-165872" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x+{sinh}^{4}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the Pythagorean identity \n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n{cosh}^{2}⁡x-{sinh}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite and calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x+{sinh}^{4}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x(1+{sinh}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {csch}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186537915 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166798 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a95e37c6-66f4-5a70-87e8-31f3694a20a4" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Hyperbolic Functions With Linear Arguments"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14f6e04e-fb88-5362-9549-483100fa12e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537271} {:answer/id #uuid "2b0b4705-45a1-5421-a9c7-5785f003fa93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537317} {:answer/id #uuid "84b7088f-f334-521c-a837-e560bd2f92fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537486} {:answer/id #uuid "d41fcdf0-a6d8-5e72-ac3e-0c3d81a914c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537648} {:answer/id #uuid "e3c2410b-a921-5ac6-85cf-3cff52fdee7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537690}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14f6e04e-fb88-5362-9549-483100fa12e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537271} :answer-field/id #uuid "65a3f970-a115-5042-b8a1-b96f4f8015c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537798}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "56c765b2-a04b-54c3-b2ad-79e20147ade9" :question/math-academy-id "q-165894" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{2+2{sinh}^{2}⁡(2x)}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n{cosh}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sinh}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\n$$\n\nSetting $\\theta =2x,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cosh}^{2}⁡(2x)-{sinh}^{2}⁡(2x) & =1 \\\\ 1+{sinh}^{2}⁡(2x) & ={cosh}^{2}⁡(2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2+2{sinh}^{2}⁡(2x)}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{2(1+{sinh}^{2}⁡(2x))}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{2{cosh}^{2}⁡(2x)}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2x)+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186537967 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166798 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a95e37c6-66f4-5a70-87e8-31f3694a20a4" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Hyperbolic Functions With Linear Arguments"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9742393d-a500-5c2a-8afe-aa9646453e0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(3x+2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537515} {:answer/id #uuid "bf467dbf-ef4a-570d-9381-8136807b7ed0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(3x+2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537600} {:answer/id #uuid "e4d1307c-5521-5cc2-9ba5-b15d1d2d5bdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sech}⁡(3x+2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537693} {:answer/id #uuid "e53abd82-d6d2-5619-b674-b500de889e2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(3x+2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537696} {:answer/id #uuid "efcebe4a-a0df-535b-8f64-7bd2e11ab057" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\operatorname{sech}⁡(3x+2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537722}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e53abd82-d6d2-5619-b674-b500de889e2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(3x+2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537696} :answer-field/id #uuid "64a7f0e3-b811-5999-abd0-ca813f824353" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537796}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c7a3ee0b-1bd5-5d07-b45d-54312bc57611" :question/math-academy-id "q-165895" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{6}{1+{sinh}^{2}⁡(3x+2)}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n{cosh}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sinh}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\n$$\n\nSetting $\\theta =3x+2,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cosh}^{2}⁡(3x+2)-{sinh}^{2}⁡(3x+2) & =1 \\\\ 1+{sinh}^{2}⁡(3x+2) & ={cosh}^{2}⁡(3x+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{6}{1+{sinh}^{2}⁡(3x+2)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{6}{{cosh}^{2}⁡(3x+2)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\int \\frac{1}{{cosh}^{2}⁡(3x+2)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\int {sech}^{2}⁡(3x+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(3x+2)+C \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(3x+2)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186537943 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166796 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "97c01757-f2bf-5b7b-b51b-ff490b54f555" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Function Using the Hyperbolic Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ba324a1-6779-572b-99bc-3815b4a02bbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537413}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ba324a1-6779-572b-99bc-3815b4a02bbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537413} :answer-field/id #uuid "6cecfe57-733c-5892-b9ce-085b5206a4dd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537804}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9ddcb9f3-50a1-505b-ae57-c8a55dc1f652" :question/math-academy-id "q-347992" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\frac{{sech}^{2}⁡x}{1-{sech}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the secant-tangent identity \n\n$$\n{sec}^{2}⁡x-1={tan}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic secant-tangent identity\n\n$$\n1-{sech}^{2}⁡x={tanh}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the integral and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\frac{{sech}^{2}⁡x}{1-{sech}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\frac{{sech}^{2}⁡x}{{tanh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}{sech}^{2}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{{tanh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\frac{1}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\frac{1}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}{csch}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x{|}_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{coth}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)-\\operatorname{coth}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{coth}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)-\\operatorname{coth}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}}-\\frac{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}-{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2+{2}^{-1}}{2-{2}^{-1}}-\\frac{4+{4}^{-1}}{4-{4}^{-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}-\\frac{17}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{15}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186537929 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166796 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "97c01757-f2bf-5b7b-b51b-ff490b54f555" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Function Using the Hyperbolic Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "620344d8-2da9-55c3-b8ec-d1845745c666" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537423}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "620344d8-2da9-55c3-b8ec-d1845745c666" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537423} :answer-field/id #uuid "52fbaaa5-e6e2-563a-8fc8-919869cd64cf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537784}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7461b1f3-1aea-5d09-ab06-c9f25cb75e4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-348024" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\frac{8\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x-8\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x{tanh}^{2}⁡x}{{sech}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the secant-tangent identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic secant-tangent identity\n\n$$\n1-{tanh}^{2}⁡x={sech}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the integral and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\frac{8\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x-8\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x{tanh}^{2}⁡x}{{sech}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\frac{8\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\cdot (1-{tanh}^{2}⁡x)}{{sech}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\frac{8\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\cdot {sech}^{2}⁡x}{{sech}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}8\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x{|}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\  & =8(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡0) \\\\  & =8(\\frac{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{0}+{e}^{-(0)}}{2}) \\\\  & =8(\\frac{2+{2}^{-1}}{2}-1) \\\\  & =8(\\frac{5}{4}-1) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186537944 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166797 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5f377f3-700a-57a9-96e5-954aed678e62" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Function Using the Hyperbolic Cosecant-Cotangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59b81cdd-3fb5-51c1-a54c-615d09c8f887" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537410}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "59b81cdd-3fb5-51c1-a54c-615d09c8f887" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537410} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc85decb-7916-5052-8222-edcbe0f6343d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537857}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9ea30f92-f367-5355-89e8-50b8c17d0449" :question/math-academy-id "q-348034" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡x+{csch}^{3}⁡x}{\\operatorname{coth}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the cotangent-cosecant identity \n\n$$\n{csc}^{2}⁡x-1={cot}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic identity\n\n$$\n1+{csch}^{2}⁡x={coth}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the integral and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡x+{csch}^{3}⁡x}{\\operatorname{coth}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(1+{csch}^{2}⁡x)}{\\operatorname{coth}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\cdot {coth}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{coth}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{coth}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x{|}_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{csch}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)-\\operatorname{csch}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csch}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)-\\operatorname{csch}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}}-\\frac{2}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{2-{2}^{-1}}-\\frac{2}{3-{3}^{-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186537975 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166797 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5f377f3-700a-57a9-96e5-954aed678e62" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Function Using the Hyperbolic Cosecant-Cotangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b3cfb59-acb3-5458-a2b9-9970c1414d6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{51}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537318}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b3cfb59-acb3-5458-a2b9-9970c1414d6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{51}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537318} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb58dffd-ddd5-56a7-b417-3fbe9d0a8b25" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537876}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d50512b3-2d0b-53b0-a169-ed8ad3f44908" :question/math-academy-id "q-348041" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}\\frac{1+{csch}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sech}⁡x{coth}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the cotangent-cosecant identity \n\n$$\n{csc}^{2}⁡x-1={cot}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic identity\n\n$$\n1+{csch}^{2}⁡x={coth}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the integral and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}\\frac{1+{csch}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sech}⁡x{coth}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}\\frac{{coth}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sech}⁡x{coth}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sech}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x{|}_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡8)-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}-{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{8-{8}^{-1}}{2}-\\frac{2-{2}^{-1}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{63}{16}-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{51}{16}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186537991 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166797 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5f377f3-700a-57a9-96e5-954aed678e62" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Function Using the Hyperbolic Cosecant-Cotangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98cbc359-2b03-5efc-8078-0d38570b0f9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537520}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98cbc359-2b03-5efc-8078-0d38570b0f9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537520} :answer-field/id #uuid "05363739-1254-5772-8cac-8bed71ed94ea" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537760}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fe6b40d3-8971-55c8-aabc-4ac03f347ec4" :question/math-academy-id "q-348060" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{x{coth}^{2}⁡x+x{csch}^{2}⁡x}{{coth}^{4}⁡x-{csch}^{4}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the cotangent-cosecant identity \n\n$$\n{csc}^{2}⁡x-{cot}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic identity\n\n$$\n{coth}^{2}⁡x-{csch}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the integral and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{x{coth}^{2}⁡x+x{csch}^{2}⁡x}{{coth}^{4}⁡x-{csch}^{4}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{x({coth}^{2}⁡x+{csch}^{2}⁡x)}{({coth}^{2}⁡x-{csch}^{2}⁡x)({coth}^{2}⁡x+{csch}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{x}{({coth}^{2}⁡x-{csch}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{x}{1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{{3}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{1}^{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186537928 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166797 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5f377f3-700a-57a9-96e5-954aed678e62" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Function Using the Hyperbolic Cosecant-Cotangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d2d80338-bd01-53da-9ff6-138404ba74a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537641}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2d80338-bd01-53da-9ff6-138404ba74a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537641} :answer-field/id #uuid "db4c0633-bccb-5234-a9ce-6b6aa8a3a63d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537864}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "70e33acb-bebf-51b2-9607-6c52a3430a18" :question/math-academy-id "q-362032" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{2}^{7}\\frac{{coth}^{4}⁡x-{csch}^{2}⁡x\\,{coth}^{2}⁡x}{{coth}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the cotangent-cosecant identity \n\n$$\n{csc}^{2}⁡x-1={cot}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic identity\n\n$$\n{coth}^{2}⁡x-{csch}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the integral and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{7}\\frac{{coth}^{4}⁡x-{csch}^{2}⁡x\\,{coth}^{2}⁡x}{{coth}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{2}^{7}\\frac{{coth}^{2}⁡x({coth}^{2}⁡x-{csch}^{2}⁡x)}{{coth}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{7}({coth}^{2}⁡x-{csch}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{7}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{|}_{2}^{7} \\\\  & =7-2 \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167408 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166795 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1df2e164-251d-5ea1-a49a-fe5bc8d67ae6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Function Using the Hyperbolic Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "421b7a92-fb82-5fac-b1cf-0b831b760fd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537365} {:answer/id #uuid "744490d1-9896-5ac5-9b5a-97aeb15a3238" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537457} {:answer/id #uuid "84be6896-bcea-56cf-8b32-6d72991af814" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537487} {:answer/id #uuid "94e81827-f57f-549f-8221-d7c1a9b3c0c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537509} {:answer/id #uuid "cc34c6ea-57ba-59bc-8e55-253f0cdf1126" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sech}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537628}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "744490d1-9896-5ac5-9b5a-97aeb15a3238" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537457} :answer-field/id #uuid "526dd014-553b-5336-80a3-305b2a62ee6b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165656}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "73150534-b7bb-5cf7-bc82-812c547a0e7e" :question/math-academy-id "q-95837" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{{coth}^{2}⁡x}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x+1}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the Pythagorean identity \n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n{cosh}^{2}⁡x-{sinh}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{coth}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the denominator and calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{coth}^{2}⁡x}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{{coth}^{2}⁡x}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x-1+1}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{{coth}^{2}⁡x}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{(\\frac{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x})}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {csch}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186537881 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166795 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1df2e164-251d-5ea1-a49a-fe5bc8d67ae6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Function Using the Hyperbolic Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "187fa676-ce69-5db4-bb19-2d5aded139fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537281} {:answer/id #uuid "3170b4a1-795f-56db-b544-2a4162816f46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537336} {:answer/id #uuid "928181c8-6764-5052-ab91-3e3d8b3ae162" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537505} {:answer/id #uuid "98505c70-07f9-5bd5-816f-3af8a4adc0d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537517} {:answer/id #uuid "a2148279-dc40-5ab9-8eaa-86cdbddf62fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537534}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98505c70-07f9-5bd5-816f-3af8a4adc0d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537517} :answer-field/id #uuid "81975dcf-378c-5d3d-b3d0-17574131c4e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537814}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "032608f7-6edc-5183-bb2d-4ede3e9c1645" :question/math-academy-id "q-96306" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int ({cosh}^{3}⁡x-{sinh}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the Pythagorean identity \n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n{cosh}^{2}⁡x-{sinh}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the denominator and calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({cosh}^{3}⁡x-{sinh}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cosh}⁡x({cosh}^{2}⁡x-{sinh}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186537925 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166795 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1df2e164-251d-5ea1-a49a-fe5bc8d67ae6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Function Using the Hyperbolic Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1734e68b-49b7-5657-a8ab-e7fd14ec92c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537276} {:answer/id #uuid "6de2d048-caee-5e8a-baf6-c37fde229e82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537442} {:answer/id #uuid "b0bcfa39-281d-566a-8e63-d65c56907c98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537568} {:answer/id #uuid "e4a99a7f-7e6c-5818-a83d-a13f8c260bfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537692} {:answer/id #uuid "faef0ce8-c4e4-53a3-9255-f04524119f87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537746}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1734e68b-49b7-5657-a8ab-e7fd14ec92c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537276} :answer-field/id #uuid "215a951f-a6c0-593d-8a1c-917970be4ccd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537771}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6bf4783e-de85-5ad3-95bc-1eadaee336f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-96307" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int (1-{sinh}^{2}⁡x{sech}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the Pythagorean identity \n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n{cosh}^{2}⁡x-{sinh}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sech}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the denominator and calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (1-{sinh}^{2}⁡x{sech}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (1-{sinh}^{2}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{{cosh}^{2}⁡x-{sinh}^{2}⁡x}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sech}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186537879 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166795 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1df2e164-251d-5ea1-a49a-fe5bc8d67ae6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Function Using the Hyperbolic Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03d5f670-27f0-5761-9a2d-2b27183ed602" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537235} {:answer/id #uuid "475499d3-6def-57f9-991e-f031b8de6556" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537378} {:answer/id #uuid "6f28b0d3-c0bf-5fe7-bb38-6f7358465bb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537444} {:answer/id #uuid "a5a81b59-7130-5b2b-ab0f-bb39e54adc0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csch}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537541} {:answer/id #uuid "ed5c2a17-7497-5332-bf7f-3b0c44e70ca7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537715}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03d5f670-27f0-5761-9a2d-2b27183ed602" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537235} :answer-field/id #uuid "588c50be-27c2-58c4-af3b-6c4e820c32d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537788}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "007da683-6a06-5103-8ccf-d7e5e491284b" :question/math-academy-id "q-96324" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1}{1-{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the Pythagorean identity \n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n{cosh}^{2}⁡x-{sinh}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite and calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{1-(1+{sinh}^{2}⁡x)}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\int \\frac{1}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\int {csch}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186537926 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166796 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "97c01757-f2bf-5b7b-b51b-ff490b54f555" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Function Using the Hyperbolic Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0035feb3-cb79-5047-8afd-04eee047fe8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csch}⁡x-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537224} {:answer/id #uuid "37efae25-c6d0-510f-8a84-02b69180da3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537343} {:answer/id #uuid "71d70417-7ef2-5fec-908e-11a78c840b3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537451} {:answer/id #uuid "a5f2dbd6-7b66-5d4d-b301-a9bd61a52a63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537542} {:answer/id #uuid "e4fc32da-9081-513c-b08e-78ad9623f9b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x+\\operatorname{sech}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537695}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71d70417-7ef2-5fec-908e-11a78c840b3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537451} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7f36f1c-baeb-5d0c-a838-31d70af0c742" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537847}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6c61796b-b24c-5403-8a9e-cd8bda63e7c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-96405" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1-\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x(1-{tanh}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the secant-tangent identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic secant-tangent identity\n\n$$\n1-{tanh}^{2}⁡x={sech}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the integral and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1-\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x(1-{tanh}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1-\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x{sech}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{{cosh}^{2}⁡(1-\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x)}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cosh}⁡x(1-\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cosh}⁡x(1-\\frac{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186537912 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166796 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "97c01757-f2bf-5b7b-b51b-ff490b54f555" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Function Using the Hyperbolic Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24173e0a-d957-5f97-a5dc-7d867846fe63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537307} {:answer/id #uuid "7178716b-d298-5054-a295-621e46c31b5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537450} {:answer/id #uuid "7bfe03f4-86e8-5f5d-a0ca-5eb20dd2e305" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537472} {:answer/id #uuid "c4de1550-9555-521c-8641-82bf296c4387" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537608} {:answer/id #uuid "ce716d8d-6f47-5a0f-9225-7a0aa1742627" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537634}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7bfe03f4-86e8-5f5d-a0ca-5eb20dd2e305" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537472} :answer-field/id #uuid "99b9d7f0-5aa1-5376-9c8e-7d9cbe16f0be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537826}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4e26e540-b6e1-55b9-88da-a99de2917513" :question/math-academy-id "q-96413" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{{sech}^{2}⁡x}{1-{sech}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the secant-tangent identity \n\n$$\n{sec}^{2}⁡x-1={tan}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic secant-tangent identity\n\n$$\n1-{sech}^{2}⁡x={tanh}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the integral and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{{sech}^{2}⁡x}{1-{sech}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{{sech}^{2}⁡x}{{tanh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{1}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{1}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{csch}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{coth}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)+\\operatorname{coth}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+1}{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-1}+\\frac{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+1}{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{3}^{2}+1}{{3}^{2}-1}+\\frac{{2}^{2}+1}{{2}^{2}-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{4}+\\frac{5}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186537949 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166796 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "97c01757-f2bf-5b7b-b51b-ff490b54f555" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Function Using the Hyperbolic Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2efeda09-6488-58c8-b51d-5cb115113e8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537330} {:answer/id #uuid "3694787f-4267-5b85-9a9d-c811b7ca8c3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537341} {:answer/id #uuid "5c2f505b-06f8-527d-b1b4-f411adee504d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537415} {:answer/id #uuid "bd388afb-e318-5bb0-ad11-815dec250e03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537596} {:answer/id #uuid "ee6a0a2b-3a0c-5024-a882-d244026f8d60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537719}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2efeda09-6488-58c8-b51d-5cb115113e8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537330} :answer-field/id #uuid "58f1aa97-2aa4-5f57-8fa7-34a54ff2bfe8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537789}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a49f44d3-1abb-5067-966c-70ae50d2155e" :question/math-academy-id "q-96429" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\frac{2-2{tanh}^{4}⁡x}{1+{tanh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the secant-tangent identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic secant-tangent identity\n\n$$\n1-{tanh}^{2}⁡x={sech}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the integral and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\frac{2-2{tanh}^{4}⁡x}{1+{tanh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\frac{1-{tanh}^{4}⁡x}{1+{tanh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\frac{(1-{tanh}^{2}⁡x)(1+{tanh}^{2}⁡x)}{1+{tanh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(1-{tanh}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{sech}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)-2\\operatorname{tanh}⁡0 \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-1}{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+1}-2\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{0}-1}{{e}^{0}+1} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{{2}^{2}-1}{{2}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186537902 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166797 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5f377f3-700a-57a9-96e5-954aed678e62" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Function Using the Hyperbolic Cosecant-Cotangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f919a0d-34cf-5c87-9355-e889ab85f2d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{17}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537297} {:answer/id #uuid "9807cc06-0ffd-5b61-ad8a-0beb97bc28e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{32}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537516} {:answer/id #uuid "9e310136-b483-5416-b6c1-753bd73f9e7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{15}{32}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537524} {:answer/id #uuid "a02ac5b9-33ba-5281-baef-70b3880d7010" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537530} {:answer/id #uuid "bb7393b4-08fb-5fb1-83f1-d004cc94717c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{60}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537594}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb7393b4-08fb-5fb1-83f1-d004cc94717c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{60}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537594} :answer-field/id #uuid "6903f8c0-f369-5cc9-83aa-7a2303f7c793" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537802}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "36b4a778-aa5a-54d9-9b61-eb9431bef188" :question/math-academy-id "q-96435" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\frac{{coth}^{4}⁡x-1}{1+{coth}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the cosecant-cotangent identity \n\n$$\n1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic cosecant-cotangent identity\n\n$$\n{coth}^{2}⁡x-1={csch}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the integral and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\frac{{coth}^{4}⁡x-1}{1+{coth}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\frac{({coth}^{2}⁡x-1)({coth}^{2}⁡x+1)}{1+{coth}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}({coth}^{2}⁡x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}{csch}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{coth}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)+\\operatorname{coth}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+1}{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}-1}+\\frac{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+1}{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{17}{15}+\\frac{5}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{60}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186537930 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166798 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a95e37c6-66f4-5a70-87e8-31f3694a20a4" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Hyperbolic Functions With Linear Arguments"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "185f59eb-c2e7-5a3f-a3b7-be2964f06456" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537280} {:answer/id #uuid "4d024158-1b7c-5e9c-9ace-8dd0eea976bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2x+1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537389} {:answer/id #uuid "ce2953bb-7aa8-5c3f-9a2d-3cafbe68e61e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2x+1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537632} {:answer/id #uuid "e3091fa4-afc7-563c-9eae-29ea28d513b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537688} {:answer/id #uuid "f153bba0-8285-5094-83d7-3b533736f1b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537727}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "185f59eb-c2e7-5a3f-a3b7-be2964f06456" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537280} :answer-field/id #uuid "571ff74d-f457-5675-971d-04ff30533fde" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537787}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7649fd25-c8c5-5938-a768-41b9d4f9aa06" :question/math-academy-id "q-96453" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{{cosh}^{3}⁡(2x-1)}{1+{sinh}^{2}⁡(2x-1)}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n{cosh}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sinh}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\n$$\n\nSetting $\\theta =2x-1,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cosh}^{2}⁡(2x-1)-{sinh}^{2}⁡(2x-1) & =1 \\\\ {cosh}^{2}⁡(2x-1) & =1+{sinh}^{2}⁡(2x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{cosh}^{3}⁡(2x-1)}{1+{sinh}^{2}⁡(2x-1)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{{cosh}^{3}⁡(2x-1)}{{cosh}^{2}⁡(2x-1)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2x-1)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186537890 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166798 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a95e37c6-66f4-5a70-87e8-31f3694a20a4" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Hyperbolic Functions With Linear Arguments"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "128c44ff-5002-57ad-a45f-4e742d10c24e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5}+2{x}^{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537263} {:answer/id #uuid "14056c1d-1503-5c16-903f-a42353bc7679" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}+2{x}^{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537266} {:answer/id #uuid "6d2f4d68-d3cb-5e06-9684-ade0a7155990" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+{x}^{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537439} {:answer/id #uuid "cdcf0690-e390-5dbd-b7f0-70fd10a011b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x}{5}+{x}^{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537630} {:answer/id #uuid "d825bf38-2203-5280-977c-5f960b7c5773" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+{x}^{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537659}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d2f4d68-d3cb-5e06-9684-ade0a7155990" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+{x}^{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537439} :answer-field/id #uuid "9dacd865-577a-5c58-b803-da35ca44d6b7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537830}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1c959d7c-d68c-591a-a3b7-ea71063de12e" :question/math-academy-id "q-96466" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int (2{cosh}^{2}⁡(5x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})+4{x}^{3}-2{sinh}^{2}⁡(5x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}))\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic Pythagorean identity\n\n$$\n{cosh}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sinh}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\n$$\n\nSetting $\\theta =5x-\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cosh}^{2}⁡(5x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})-{sinh}^{2}⁡(5x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (2{cosh}^{2}⁡(5x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})+4{x}^{3}-2{sinh}^{2}⁡(5x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}))\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2[{cosh}^{2}⁡(5x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})-{sinh}^{2}⁡(5x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})]+4{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (2+4{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int 2\\cdot \\text{d}x+\\int 4{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2x+{x}^{4}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186537985 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166798 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a95e37c6-66f4-5a70-87e8-31f3694a20a4" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Hyperbolic Functions With Linear Arguments"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7dc7a7fb-89cd-51cd-aab3-8e7b474b89ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{coth}⁡(7x-2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537475} {:answer/id #uuid "a9b368e1-f7b0-5dd8-92cb-a1654e1ce507" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{coth}⁡(7x-2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537548} {:answer/id #uuid "d97a0c7a-a10a-50ef-8a0c-e16fb5ef9b78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{csch}⁡(7x-2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537661} {:answer/id #uuid "dd74e5e2-9f80-5316-85b3-b0b8a53ad347" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{csch}⁡(7x-2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537675} {:answer/id #uuid "f46ac096-0fba-5cb8-8f28-45008d53cdf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{csch}⁡(7x-2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537732}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd74e5e2-9f80-5316-85b3-b0b8a53ad347" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{csch}⁡(7x-2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537675} :answer-field/id #uuid "919f8a47-bdd5-52ef-8d35-92386471095f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537819}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f321e82d-23c7-5f15-828b-dbb232e439d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-96522" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{{csch}^{3}⁡(7x-2)+\\operatorname{csch}⁡(7x-2)}{\\operatorname{coth}⁡(7x-2)}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the cosecant-cotangent identity \n\n$$\n1+{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta ={csc}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic cosecant-cotangent identity\n\n$$\n{coth}^{2}⁡\\theta -1={csch}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nSetting $\\theta =7x-2,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{coth}^{2}⁡(7x-2)-1 & ={csch}^{2}⁡(7x-2) \\\\ {coth}^{2}⁡(7x-2) & ={csch}^{2}⁡(7x-2)+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{csch}^{3}⁡(7x-2)+\\operatorname{csch}⁡(7x-2)}{\\operatorname{coth}⁡(7x-2)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡(7x-2)[{csch}^{2}⁡(7x-2)+1]}{\\operatorname{coth}⁡(7x-2)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡(7x-2){coth}^{2}⁡(7x-2)}{\\operatorname{coth}⁡(7x-2)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{csch}⁡(7x-2)\\operatorname{coth}⁡(7x-2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{csch}⁡(7x-2)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
